  "id": "schizotypy",
  "term": "schizotypy",
  "definition": "Schizotypy refers to relatively stable subclinical traits involving odd or eccentric beliefs, speech, and behavior. These traits are commonly grouped into interpersonal difficulties, cognitive-perceptual unusualness, and disorganization, and are often understood either as part of the schizophrenia spectrum or as latent traits linked to vulnerability to schizophrenia.",
